modifying the same file. The orchestrator executes sequentially based on dependencies, so if both tasks could run in parallel without that constraint, they'd conflict when writing to main.go. Task 3 must wait for task 2 to finish.\n\nNow I'm checking against the requirement constraints—the spec says code tasks should target 5-8 requirements each, but I've only allocated 3-4 per task. Let me reconsider whether I'm distributing the requirements correctly. , I can get 4 task requirements per task. But P9 calls for 5-8 requirements, which creates a genuine conflict.\n\nThe hard constraint of 4 SRD sub-requirements per task takes precedence over the guideline, so I should stick with that limit. Adding extra non-SRD requirements would artificially inflate the count, which the constraint explicitly warns against. I think 3-4 requirements per task is the right approach given these constraints.\n\nFor acceptance criteria, P9 suggests 5-8, and my tasks currently have 4-5. I should expand those to hit the target more consistently.\n\nNow I'm deciding on reference materials. The CLAUDE.md file covers the patterns well, but a concrete example would be helpful. cmd/chmod is a good fit since it's in the same domain as shred and already implemented. For the chroot task, the existing codebase already has the reference implementation, so I don't need to add anything there.\n\nLet me finalize the output with thorough acceptance criteria across all tasks.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":45323,"cache_read_input_tokens":11845,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":45323},"output_tokens":25,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8abd0c7f-f561-4a92-b22a-6664839a2455","uuid":"0eab8b5a-c983-4385-acd5-a95c9af53bbb"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01JeGQzgGeCDCPW5TbdteRJn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Unix utilities lack formal specs accessible to implementers. This project derives formal specs from C source, generates Go implementations via AI, and verifies parity through differential testing against Homebrew GNU binaries.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract, specify, synthesize, verify). Human writes SRDs/use cases. mage-claude-orchestrator generates Go. pkg/testutils runs differential tests comparing Go against GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Current state**: 33 releases (00.0-15.0), all spec_complete. Generation run 44 in progress. Recent commits: srd100-chroot R1.1-R1.3 (task 5585), srd097-who (task 5584). requirement_states shows remaining \"ready\" requirements across SRDs 004, 099-114.\n\n**Current release**: rel12.0 (file security and installation) is the earliest release with ready requirements:\n- srd100-chroot: R2.1, R2.2, R2.3 remain (R1.x done in task 5585)\n- srd099-shred: all 11 requirements ready (R1.1-R1.4, R2.1-R2.4, R3.1-R3.3)\n- srd101-install: all 11 requirements ready\n\n## Weight Budget Verification\n\n```\nTask 0 (shred contract): No SRD requirement weights -- contract task\nTask 1 (chroot R2.1-R2.3): R2.1(w=1) + R2.2(w=1) + R2.3(w=1) = 3 ≤ 4 ✓\nTask 2 (shred R1.1-R1.4): R1.1(w=1) + R1.2(w=1) + R1.3(w=1) + R1.4(w=1) = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\nTask 3 (shred R2.1-R2.4): R2.1(w=1) + R2.2(w=1) + R2.3(w=1) + R2.4(w=1) = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\n```\n\nWeights assumed default 1; no weight overrides in project context for rel12.0 SRDs.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\n1. rel12.0 is earliest incomplete release with ready requirements\n2. srd100-chroot has 3 remaining requirements, package exists from task 5585 -- no contract needed\n3. srd099-shred is a new package (not started) -- needs contract before implementation\n4. With 4-task limit: complete chroot (1 task), start shred (contract + 2 implementation tasks)\n5. srd101-install and shred R3.x deferred to next batch\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/shred (contract) -- srd099-shred\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd099-shred.yaml (all requirements and acceptance criteria for shred)\n      - cmd/chmod/main.go (reference cmd/ package pattern -- flag parsing, SIGPIPE handler, exit codes)\n      - pkg/sys/sigpipe.go (SIGPIPE handler import path)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/shred/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: \"Package main with flag definitions, main() skeleton, and stub functions for all shred operations\"\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Define all flag variables matching every flag specified in srd099-shred with correct Go types and default values\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement main() with sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler(), flag.Parse(), argument validation that prints usage to stderr and exits 1 on no file arguments, and a dispatch loop over file arguments\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Define stub functions for each operation required by the SRD -- each stub must have the correct signature and return nil or a placeholder error so the package compiles\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Include --help and --version output matching GNU shred format with all flags documented\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the start of main per project shared protocol\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Use Go standard library flag package for command-line argument parsing\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"All stub functions must compile cleanly -- the contract must pass go build and go vet\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"cmd/shred/main.go exists with package main declaration\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go build ./cmd/shred/ succ